BEHAVIOR write-file-all

DESCRIPTION
  Writes length bytes of data to path, creating/truncating it (flags 3 =
  write|create). Returns the number of bytes written. Convenience wiring over
  open/write/close.

CONTRACT
  INPUT path string
  INPUT data bytes 65536
  INPUT length int 8
  OUTPUT bytes_written int 8
  REQUIRES open@7d62cd96 write@874767ff close@d4ba30e5
  GUARANTEES writes_output

HASH b17d9aa8

COMPOSITION
  outf = CALL open path 3
  wr = CALL write outf.fd data length
  cl = CALL close outf.fd
  DISCARD cl.status
  SET bytes_written wr.bytes_written
END
